[00:04.000]
[00:07.000]And now, the end is near;
[00:12.000]And so I face the final curtain.
[00:19.000]My friend, I'll say it clear,
[00:24.000]Ill state my case, of which i'm certain.
[00:32.000]I've lived a life thats full.
[00:38.000]I've traveled each and every highway;
[00:44.000]And more, much more than this,
[00:50.000]I did it my way.
[00:57.000]Regrets, I've had a few;
[01:03.000]But then again, too few to mention.
[01:09.000]I did what I had to do
[01:15.000]And saw it through without exemption.
[01:22.000]I planned each charted course;
[01:28.000]Each careful step along the byway,
[01:35.000]But more, much more than this,
[01:40.000]I did it my way.
[01:46.000]Yes, there were times, I'm sure you knew
[01:53.000]When I bit off more than I could chew.
[02:00.000]But through it all, when there was doubt,
[02:06.000]I ate it up and spit it out.
[02:11.998]I faced it all and I stood tall;
[02:18.998]And did it my way.
[02:24.998]I've loved, I've laughed and cried.
[02:30.998]I've had my fill; my share of losing.
[02:37.998]And now, as tears subside,
[02:43.998]I find it all so amusing.
[02:50.998]To think I did all that;
[02:55.998]And may I say - not in a shy way,
[03:03.998]"Oh no, oh no not me,
[03:08.998]I did it my way".
[03:14.998]For what is a man, what has he got?
[03:21.998]If not himself, then he has naught.
[03:27.998]To say the things he truly feels;
[03:34.998]And not the words of one who kneels.
[03:41.998]The record shows I took the blows -
[03:48.998]And did it my way!
